{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734683-shattered-dreams-some-inconsistencies-regarding-the-ananasi","id":734683,"title":"Shattered Dreams: some inconsistencies regarding the Ananasi","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-28T07:39:29-07:00","id":734683,"title":"Shattered Dreams: some inconsistencies regarding the Ananasi","content":"The unedited draft states at multiple times that the Ananasi are spreading the Weaver's influence. Chapter 2 furthermore states that they are doing so because their Queen is inside her opal prison and so they must obey.<br /> In W20 Changing Breed 20, though, the authors went with the old version from the Ananasi's own breedbook: the Weaver tossed the opal to the Wyrm, and it was it who forced the Ananasi into service.<br /> Furthermore that had ended well into prehistory - at the time of the Second War of Rage the Ananasi should not have been doing the Weaver or the Wyrm's will anymore, but they were already organized into the Triumvirate.<br /> There's also the fact that all of this happened after the massacre of hte Neanderthal, but that's info taken from the old breedbook so it's not an inconsistency, rather a rewrite. But Shattered Dreams shouldn't conflict so grossly with a book published not a year before in the same line.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T08:04:44-07:00","id":734771,"title":"","content":"Agreed - few things are more vexing than continuity mistakes in books published nearly together. Did you post this on the kickstarter page (or wherever they're collecting feedback on the document right now) as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T08:13:20-07:00","id":734814,"title":"","content":"Nope, that's a very good idea. This is the first place I thought of. I'll get to it.<br /> <br /> EDIT it seems like I ca't comment without backing first, which for now I didn't do. Well, I guess this post gives enough visibility to the issue, or maybe I'll post a comment on the OPP blog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","user":"Vidyaraja","date":". 10-28-2015, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T16:20:49-07:00","id":736135,"title":"","content":"This is covered in the book. its not a continuity issue its a &quot;modern changing breeds do not have a 100 percent view of history&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T17:08:15-07:00","id":736286,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I saw that, so I refrained from pointing out other &quot;inconsistencies&quot; that could be attributed to that (one comes to mind: in Tribebook: White Howlers it's stated that during the Ice Age the White Howlers, Fianna and Get of Fenris were already distinct tribes with their own totems, which contraddicts accounts in Shattered Dreams)<br /> But I think the Ananasi would be fairly sure wether they were in thrall to Wyrm or Weaver. They would certainly know if in the fifteenth century they were organized in the Triumvirate or still serving a single Triatic aspect. Furthermore the discrepancy is never addressed; SD states there's an opal prison, so that part is true, but then changes one major actor for the other, and without further explanation it seems more an oversight than a reveal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T18:15:41-07:00","id":736423,"title":"","content":"There's also multiple references to the Camazotz burning from gold, not silver, which is in contraddiction with W20 Changing Breed again - and doesn't make a lick of sense.<br /> The writer(s) of this book would benefit from a thorough reading of W20 Changing Breed, I think.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T18:32:22-07:00","id":736448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vidyaraja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734683-shattered-dreams-some-inconsistencies-regarding-the-ananasi?p=736423#post736423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also multiple references to the Camazotz burning from gold, not silver, which is in contraddiction with W20 Changing Breed again - and doesn't make a lick of sense.<br /> The writer(s) of this book would benefit from a thorough reading of W20 Changing Breed, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a number of them wrote for it, so that's probably not the problem. I'd be quicker to blame very little sleep, any day, any time. It's a killer. A lot of the accounts of the historical battles can get as confusing and dry as the landmark battles in Wars of Reaving, though, where there's a long list of characters and a rather unegaging blow by blow of what happens to whom by who or what, like the last part of Wolfpack by Sabaton, without the music.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T18:32:43-07:00","id":736449,"title":"","content":"Now if only there was a thread where the writers are talking to people about the book two days before the kick stater launched....if only...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T22:36:16-07:00","id":737016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vidyaraja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734683-shattered-dreams-some-inconsistencies-regarding-the-ananasi?p=736286#post736286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I saw that, so I refrained from pointing out other &quot;inconsistencies&quot; that could be attributed to that (one comes to mind: in Tribebook: White Howlers it's stated that during the Ice Age the White Howlers, Fianna and Get of Fenris were already distinct tribes with their own totems, which contraddicts accounts in Shattered Dreams)<br /> But I think the Ananasi would be fairly sure wether they were in thrall to Wyrm or Weaver. They would certainly know if in the fifteenth century they were organized in the Triumvirate or still serving a single Triatic aspect. Furthermore the discrepancy is never addressed; SD states there's an opal prison, so that part is true, but then changes one major actor for the other, and without further explanation it seems more an oversight than a reveal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes in Tribebook White Howlers the Tribe before it fell believed itself a distinct entity from those other point. Amazingly they were wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T03:50:33-07:00","id":737541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734683-shattered-dreams-some-inconsistencies-regarding-the-ananasi?p=736449#post736449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now if only there was a thread where the writers are talking to people about the book two days before the kick stater launched....if only...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, okay, I didn't know writers posted in that thread. Heading there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T05:44:44-07:00","id":741444,"title":"","content":"Thanks for bringing this up. Sadly, we're all busy on multiple books and sometimes continuity errors do sneak through --- even when the same person created the references in each book. Fortunately, this is why we released the draft to the public, so we catch bugs like this when we can fix them, rather than when they're printed on the page.<br /> <br /> <b>Ananasi</b><br /> <br /> Queen Ananasa's prison is indeed held by the Wyrm, not the Weaver. While this does change their motivations through much of the First War of Rage, it does not impact many of their actions in the First War of Rage. While the Wyrm holds on to the opal prison, the werespiders do their best to embody the Wyrm of Balance (in much the same way as the modern Hatar) in the hopes that they may one day free their Queen. They don't always get it right, especially as the Corruptor Wyrm is influencing what information they get.<br /> <br /> By the time of the Second War of Rage they are indeed organised in the Triumvirate; references will be updated &amp; changed to reflect that.<br /> <br /> <b>Camazotz</b><br /> <br /> The were-bats do indeed burn at the touch of silver, not gold. The big dust-up in the Poison period instead becomes about the other breeds believing that the Corax and Camazotz somehow gave humans the secrets of the poison metals \u2014 the other Changing Breeds can fight, while Gaia's messengers are so much steaming confetti if they piss off the wrong Changing Breed. The theory (spoken loudest by the Garou and Bastet) goes that the conflicts of history have left the Messengers fearing for their safety should the other shapeshifters take a dislike to them, and so they found poisons that would burn the Changing Breeds. Naturally, this paranoia kicks off into open war, leaving raven and bat to work together in developing asymmetric warfare.<br /> <br /> These changes will be put into the draft when we incorporate the last chapter (the War of Tears and the War of Dragons). While I can't guarantee that this will be before the end of the Kickstarter I will make sure that the updated draft is made public, either by updating the current file or sending out a new link.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T06:18:20-07:00","id":741558,"title":"","content":"Stew, can I just say that I really appreciate the fact that not only did you come down here to tell us, but that you also provided us with a well thought out response that included previously known information and new stuff that gels with it. Kudos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T06:32:30-07:00","id":741580,"title":"","content":"I agree. The fact that the writers are available to engage the community, give clarifications and occasionally admit mistakes and take steps to correct them puts OPP's works among the best in the industry. Thank you for taking the time to answer me and thank you for the work you put (and will be putting) in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T11:54:48-07:00","id":742419,"title":"","content":"Glad I could be of assistance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>--<br /> Stew Wilson<br /> Werewolf Developer<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/index.php?manufacturers_id=3820&amp;affiliate_id=81234\" target=\"_blank\">My games. Buy them.</a><br /> The maturity of the developer might go down as well as up. Bum. Willy. Fart. Nietzche.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28-digitalraven","name":"DigitalRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T20:26:35-07:00","id":743649,"title":"","content":"That is a big relief Stew! Thank you very much for talking with us here too -- I didn't back Shattered Dreams but when it's out and reviewed I may get it then. It's really wonderful to be able to engage with the writers outside of the KS communication channels.* (It's also wonderful that I can edit my posts on here.)<br /> <br /> I was confused by the gold thing because I thought I remembered Camazotz burning from silver in CB20, and it sure seems inconsistent with all the previous material talking up their relationship with Luna. I was willing to give it a chance if it had a good explanation and made possible some interesting stories for the &quot;Poison Period&quot;, but if it isn't necessary for the Shattered Dreams story/stories to work I hope it's changed back to silver.<br /> <br /> I'm not bothered if the grandiose self-congratulating histories of the Garou tribes aren't 100% accurate. Nor by the revelation that the Fera breeds also committed their share of crimes in the Wars of Rage. Changing-Breed histories are all full of arrogance, bias, prejudice, and self-aggrandizing, so it isn't surprising to see suggestions (objective or subjective) that they aren't entirely accurate. (Nor would I be surprised by different branches of a far-flung tribe disagreeing over their history or origin myth.)<br /> <br /> I didn't catch the Ananasi inconsistencies but I'm glad that they weren't intentional. Retcons in general... bug me. Except when the earlier continuity was self-contradictory or just exceptionally dumb.<br /> <br /> <br /> *KS's change of ToS a few years back disturbed me enough that I want to delete my account there. I'm not down with forced-arbitration, waiving-my-Constitutional-rights-to-trial-by-jury contracts. I just have to wait until Exalted 3E is well and truly complete. Which means not backing anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-30-2015, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}